Doing the Valkyrie Quest, carrying a nice fat bag of holding. Even
with stuff stashed in three chests around the dungeon I'm still
burdened, and I just reached Lord Surtur's lair.  So I go up one level
and drop the bag .... "The bag falls down the stairs. You are
unencumbered."  Uh-oh...

Go downstairs, NO BAG.  WHERE'D IT GO???  I had my holy water in
there, my Fire Brand and Magicbane (from a bones pile), about 20
scrolls and 15 potions and 10 wands, some other junk ... noooooo.....

Maybe it rolled into the lava. Will it burn up and destroy all my
stuff?

Well, I'm wearing enough armor, carrying +2 Mjollnir, eight +3 elven
daggers and a few wands, and my beloved pet Billy the Balrog is
hanging around too. We'll kill Lord Surtur and everyone else and then
hunt for the bag.  So I do that... twice I step into lava, but Odin
smiles on me and puts me back on solid ground.  Got the Orb and Bell
now ... oh good, the Orb is a crystal ball, let's use it.

There's my bag! ... in the lava, right next to the stairs.  I'll just
zap this wand of cold ... NO CHARGES???

zap, zap, zap, zap ... 50 turns later still no cold.  So I'm carrying
one magic lamp and I've found two others in the dungeon as well. I'll
burn one on a wish for a wand of cold. (Maybe I should have wished for
scrolls of charging. Oh well).

The first magic lamp generates a disturbed genie!  At least she's
peaceful...

Go back up to the Home level. Yeah, yeah, you're happy I defeated the
Dark One, pipe down already. The second magic lamp is in this chest
here ... whew, I get a wish.

Back to the bottom, freeze the lava where the bag was, now dig ...
"The hole fills with lava! You'd be burnt to a crisp if you tried
grabbing stuff." Oh shit ... scroll of teleport, whew.

Freeze ALL AROUND the square where the bag was, now dig again ...
YAAY! The bag's there and nothing inside is burnt!! Pretty weird
considering it was greased, too .. you'd think the grease would catch
fire, but no.

Boy, that were a close one!


